# Written before the Dockerfile, deliberately: the build context is uploaded to
# the daemon before any instruction runs, so an unignored data/app.db or
# .env.local is already off the machine whether or not a COPY references it.

# Version control and editor/tooling state
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.codex
.cursor
.impeccable
.superpowers

# Reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image
node_modules
.next
out
build

# Runtime state. A developer's database must never enter a build context.
data
*.db
*.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Secrets. .env.example is documentation and is deliberately NOT excluded —
# the negation must follow the wildcard to survive it.
.env
.env.*
# The generated local development environment. Covered by `.env.*`, named for
# the same reason .gitignore names it: the builder stage runs `COPY . .`, so a
# file that slipped past this list is baked into an image layer.
.env.dev.local
!.env.example
data-info.txt
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
service-account*.json

# Regenerated in the image by scripts/copy-tinymce.mjs. Copying the developer's
# build would ship whatever version happened to be on their machine.
public/assets/tinymce

# Logs and caches
*.log
logs
coverage
.cache
*.tsbuildinfo

# Not needed to build or run the application
docs
tests
vitest.config.ts
README.md

# Private developer documentation and the agent-facing root documents. These
# live in dev-docs/ (Phase 9.10E); the three filenames below are kept as a
# defensive rule so a tool that recreates one at the root cannot put it into a
# build context.
dev-docs
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
PROJECT_DOCUMENTATION.md

# Repository governance and GitHub configuration. These describe contributing
# to FlowCMS, not running it, and changing one should not invalidate a layer.
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CHANGELOG.md

# The scaffolder and the template it carries. `packages/flowcms` IS needed —
# the application imports the built theme contract from it — but create-flowcms
# only generates other projects, and its `template/` directory is a second full
# copy of this repository. Copying it would roughly double the build context.
packages/create-flowcms

# Local pack artifacts
*.tgz

# Docker's own files — changing compose.yml should not bust the build cache
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yml
compose.*.yml

# Package build output: regenerated inside the image by scripts/build-package.mjs
# and scripts/build-example-theme.mjs. Copying a developer's would ship whatever
# was on their machine and bust the layer cache on every local rebuild.
packages/*/dist
